Production Improvements

For an enterprise-grade system, I recommend a few enhancements beyond the basic design:

1. Store a Hash Instead of the Raw Refresh Token

Instead of:

token = eyJhbGc...

Store:

tokenHash = SHA-256(refreshToken)

If the database is compromised, attackers cannot directly use the stored refresh tokens.

2. Add Device Information
private String deviceName;

private String deviceId;

private String ipAddress;

private String userAgent;

This enables features like:

"Logged in from Chrome on Windows"
"Sign out from this device"
Suspicious login detection
3. Replace revoked with Status (Optional)

Instead of a boolean:

public enum RefreshTokenStatus {
    ACTIVE,
    REVOKED,
    EXPIRED
}

This provides richer state management if your application grows.

4. Use a Shared Auditable Base Class

Rather than repeating:

createdAt
updatedAt

create:

@MappedSuperclass
public abstract class AuditableEntity {
    // createdAt, updatedAt, @PrePersist, @PreUpdate
}

Then:

public class RefreshToken extends AuditableEntity {
    ...
}

This keeps all entities consistent and reduces duplication.







