Why 64 Bytes?
64 bytes

↓

512 bits

↓

Very High Entropy

↓

Practically Impossible to Guess

The generated token looks like:

8E7kK2f9lR4vPq6N...

instead of sequential IDs or predictable UUIDs.

Why Base64 URL Encoder?

Standard Base64 produces characters like:

+
/
=

These require URL encoding.

Using:

Base64.getUrlEncoder()

produces URL-safe tokens:

A-Z
a-z
0-9
-
_




